    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="1439" n="1423" sameAs="frus:frus1951v01/pg1423"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">394.31/9–2951: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The United States</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">GATT</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Delegation to the Secretary of
                            State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Geneva</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1951-09-29">September 29,
                        1951</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    Tagg 49. Fol delivered Exec Sec 10:40 a. m.,
                    Geneva time, Sept 29:</p>
                <p>“My dear Mr. Executive Secretary: This is to inform you that the Government of
                    the US invokes its right under the second paragraph of the operative part of the
                    declaration by the CPs of September 27, 1951, and
                    hereby suspends, effective immediately and until further notice, the obligations
                    of the US with respect to Czechoslovakia under the GATT.</p>
                <p>“Sincerely yours, Willard L. Thorp, Chairman, USDel Sixth Session of CPs to the
                        GATT”.</p>
                <p>Anticipate circulation of GATT doc in Geneva and
                    release to press in Washington.</p>
                <p>Pls advise date publicity and text any covering release.</p>
            </div>
